Package: spifa
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Item Factor Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Encoding: UTF-8
Authors@R: c(
    person(c("Erick", "A."), "Chacón-Montalván", , "erick.chaconmontalvan@wur.nl",
        role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8068-1034")),
    person("Emanuele", "Giorgi", email = "e.giorgi@lancaster.ac.uk", role = "ctb"),
    person("Benjamin M.", "Taylor", email = "b.taylor1@lancaster.ac.uk", role = "ctb"))
Description: Fits item factor analysis models for binary responses using full
    Bayesian inference via Gibbs sampling and auxiliary variables with a
    probit link function. In addition to standard exploratory and
    confirmatory item factor analysis, the latent factors can be modelled as
    a multivariate Gaussian process to capture spatial dependence, allowing
    users to fit and predict spatially-referenced constructs such as
    ideological positions or socio-economic indices.
